    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": null,
    "text": "2.8. Updates: You can update existing rows using the UPDATE command. Suppose you discover the temperature readings are all off by 2 degrees after November 28. You can correct the data as follows:",
    "dom_ids": [
      "readar-node-0001",
      "readar-node-0002"
    ],
    "merge": "heading_fold",
    "chapter": "tutorial-update",
    "id": "tutorial-update__node_0001"
  },
  {
    "type": "code",
    "level": null,
    "text": "2.8. Updates: UPDATE weather\n    SET temp_hi = temp_hi - 2,  temp_lo = temp_lo - 2\n    WHERE date > '1994-11-28';",
    "dom_ids": [
      "readar-node-0001",
      "readar-node-0003"
    ],
    "merge": "heading_fold",
    "chapter": "tutorial-update",
    "id": "tutorial-update__node_0002"
  },
  {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "level": null,
    "text": "2.8. Updates: Look at the new state of the data:",
    "dom_ids": [
      "readar-node-0001",
      "readar-node-0004"
    ],
    "merge": "heading_fold",
    "chapter": "tutorial-update",
    "id": "tutorial-update__node_0003"
  },
  {
    "type": "code",
    "level": null,
    "text": "2.8. Updates: SELECT * FROM weather;\n\n     city      | temp_lo | temp_hi | prcp |    date\n---------------+---------+---------+------+------------\n San Francisco |      46 |      50 | 0.25 | 1994-11-27\n San Francisco |      41 |      55 |    0 | 1994-11-29\n Hayward       |      35 |      52 |      | 1994-11-29\n(3 rows)",
    "dom_ids": [
